Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Aanika Asnani
Title: Strengthening Tribal Consultation in the New Markets Tax Credit Program: A Policy Brief
Abstract: The New Markets Tax Credit (NMTC) Program, administered by the U.S. Department of the Treasury's Community Development Financial Institutions (CDFI) Fund, was established to stimulate private investment in economically distressed communities through federal tax incentives. The program, since its inception in 2000, has generated over $81 billion in tax credit allocation authority, at 8:1 ratio. This policy paper argues that the principal governance challenge within the current NMTC framework is not the participation of non-Native CDEs themselves, but rather the absence of structured consultation between non-Native CDEs and Native stakeholders during investment decision-making. After considering the feasibility of implementation, institutional capacity, and the likely impact of the policy, the paper suggests creating a formalized consultation arrangement between existing Native CDEs and existing non-Native CDEs.
Journal: Global Confluence Review
Volume: 1
Issue: 2
Year: 2026
Month: July
File-URL: https://www.globalconfluencereview.in/Issue2-Vol1%5BJuly-Sep2026%5D/Aanika_Asnani.pdf
