Keywords: New Markets Tax Credit (NMTC); Community Development Financial Institutions Fund (CDFI Fund); Community Development Entities (CDEs); Tribal Economic Development; Tribal Consultation; Public Policy
Classification-JEL: H25; R58; H71

Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Aaryan Bakshi
Title: Low-Cost Carriers and the Transformation of the Indian Domestic Aviation Sector
Abstract: This paper attempts to describe the growth and impact of low-cost carriers (LCCs) in India's domestic aviation industry. It charts how the LCC model grew in tandem with the evolution of airline involvement, domestic connections, passenger usage, and operational, safety, and pricing systems. Secondary data gathered in this study include information from aviation authorities, airline disclosures, published data sets, flight tracking data, and some academic and industry literature. The analysis span is 2000-2024 with selected observations from 2025 to note the recent operational and regulatory developments. The results reveal a sector that has been affected by competitive low operating costs, network expansion, shifting market participation, and network model variations alongside the ongoing regulatory oversight.
