Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Aditya Gupta
Title: Policy Paper Closing the Last Mile in Deceased Organ Donation in India: Policy Frameworks, Grassroots Barriers and a District-Level Referral and Family Navigation Model
Abstract: India has an extensive legal and institutional framework for organ donation: the Transplantation of Human Organs and Tissues Act recognises brain-stem death, a national network of transplant organisations coordinates allocation, and over five lakh citizens have registered Aadhaar-verified pledges since 2023. Yet deceased donation remains below one donor per million population, against about 48 per million in Spain. This paper argues that the shortfall is one of conversion, not willingness. The paper recommends a District Organ Donation Referral and Family Navigation Framework combining ICU identification triggers, a one-call referral line, shared rapid-response coordinators, multilingual family materials and stage-by-stage reporting with feedback to hospitals.
Journal: Global Confluence Review
