Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Aryavir Gulati
Title: Evaluating Overvalued vs Undervalued F1 Drivers of the 2025 Formula 1 season
Abstract: In F1, driver skill plays only a minor role in the results that they achieve on track; car performance plays a much bigger part, and driver salaries vary significantly from under $1 million to over $60 million per year. This study compares driver salary to on-track performance for the entire 2025 season (24 races + 6 sprint races, N = 21 drivers). On-track performance was defined as head-to-head win percentage against a teammate from the same team. Data were analyzed with robust regression in Stata. The results showed that salary was a statistically significant predictor of head-to-head performance (b = 1.09, p = .009), while age was not a significant predictor (p = .321).
Journal: Global Confluence Review
