Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Hargun Kaur
Title: Algorithms That Manufacture Desire: How Social Media Curation Co-Produces Luxury Taste Among Generation Z
Abstract: Much of the research on digital consumer culture holds that algorithmically curated social media shapes what Generation Z finds desirable and normal in luxury fashion. This study tests the short-run version of the claim with an experiment. Seventy-eight adults aged 18 to 28, recruited online, mostly female and mostly living in India, were each randomly assigned to one of three versions of a survey. Composite scores did not differ detectably across conditions, F(2, 75) = 0.13, p = .88. In this sample, one brief exposure to curated luxury content produced no detectable shift in luxury taste. Whether luxury taste forms through repeated exposure remains a hypothesis for longitudinal research.
Journal: Global Confluence Review
