Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Ravi Shingadia
Title: The Impact of Instagram Followers, Age, Brand Endorsements, and Matches Played on Professional Football Players' Market Value
Abstract: In today's day and age, professional footballers are no longer just meant to be valued for their performance on the field but also for their off the field attributes such as their age, experience, social media presence, and marketability. This study analyzes if any relationship exists between these variables and market value. A multiple linear regression model was estimated in STATA MP 18. The regression model was statistically significant, F(5, 475) = 311.15, p < .001, and explained approximately 76.6% of the variance in market value. Market value was positively predicted by number of matches played, number of Instagram followers, and the country development category.
