Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Ridit Aggarwal
Title: A Qualitative Systematic Review of Industrial Corrosive Substances in India Using the PRISMA Framework
Abstract: This study compares and analyses the regulation, supply chain and usage of industrial corrosive substances in India, with particular focus on their accessibility, control and safe handling across the different stages of the supply chain. Despite the development of regulatory and safety frameworks, the reviewed literature indicates gaps in the extent to which these controls are implemented across manufacturing, transportation, storage, purchasing and end-use. A qualitative systematic review approach is used to adhere to the PRISMA methodology. After screening, a total of 186 studies were identified from the Scopus database and analysed by thematic synthesis.
