Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Shambhavi Mittal
Title: Factors Affecting Consumer Food Price in India: An Econometric Analysis
Abstract: This study examines the determinants of food price movements in India with the aim of assessing the influence of exchange rates, crude oil prices, monetary policy, and fertilizer prices on the Consumer Food Price Index (CFPI). The study adopts a quantitative secondary-data time-series econometric design using annual data for the period 2000-2025. The data was analyzed using descriptive statistics, Pearson pairwise correlation, multiple linear regression and multicollinearity diagnostics in STATA. The final regression results indicate that fertilizer WPI has a coefficient of 1.650269 and a P-value of 0.000 and EUR/INR exchange rate has a coefficient of 1.239716 with a P-value of 0.000 are statistically significant at 5%. The final model reports an R-squared of 0.9847.
