Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Suryavir Bhandari
Title: Sport Sponsorship, Branding and Marketing: A Bibliometric Analysis Using VOSviewer
Abstract: This review presents a bibliometric map of the sport sponsorship, branding and marketing literature indexed in Scopus between 2000 and 2026. A systematic search restricted to journal articles in the business, social science, economics and humanities subject areas returned 211 documents, authored by 506 researchers across 140 journals and accumulating 3,667 citations. Five VOSviewer analyses were used to map this corpus: co-authorship among authors, organisations and countries; co-occurrence of all keywords; and bibliographic coupling among documents. The findings indicate that sponsorship value depends on brand-property congruence and sustained relational alignment rather than exposure alone.
