Template-Type: ReDIF-Article 1.0
Author-Name: Vihana Gaidhani
Title: Assessing Public Awareness and Perceived Effectiveness of Sustainability Initiatives in Indian Railways
Abstract: Indian Railways (IR) has committed to achieving net-zero carbon emissions by 2030 through large-scale electrification, renewable energy integration, and allied environmental programs. Yet the extent to which passengers are aware of, and perceive value in, these initiatives remains empirically underexplored. Descriptive demographic differences were observed in this exploratory, non-probability sample: respondents aged 23-27 reported the lowest awareness across all initiative categories, and awareness levels varied by gender across initiative themes.
